# Guardian of the Great Door {W}{W}, 4/4 flying: "As an additional cost to cast this spell, tap four untapped artifacts,
# creatures, and/or lands you control." (CR 601.2b, 118.3) The {W}{W} comes from Mox Pearl and Black Lotus, with plenty to
# spare, so only the taps matter. Bot1 has an untapped Deafening Silence too, an enchantment, which is none of the three
# types and so is never among the four. With Mox Jet, Mox Ruby and Mox Sapphire untapped but nothing else tappable of
# Bot1's (Bot2's Ornithopter and Mox Pearl, already tapped, don't count) the cast is refused: three are one short. Once
# Bot1 has its own Ornithopter (an artifact creature, summoning sick: tapping it is a cost, not its {T}, CR 302.6) the
# four may not be an already tapped Mox Pearl or the Deafening Silence, and are the Moxen and the Ornithopter; Bot2's stays
# untapped. Exactly four are tapped: a Forest played too, which could have been one of them, stays untapped.

